<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>This project builds an <strong>automated, end-to-end AI system for cervical cancer cell detection and classification</strong> using the SIPaKMeD public medical dataset. The system processes raw microscope slide images and produces per-cell clinical diagnoses within seconds.</p>
<p>The defining architectural innovation is a <strong>Super Ensemble Meta-Learner</strong>: a majority-voting system combining three independently trained gradient-boosted / tree-based models (XGBoost, LightGBM, Random Forest), each receiving <strong>51 biologically-derived features</strong> extracted by a Deep Learning preprocessing chain (YOLOv8 → U-Net → EfficientNet-B0).</p>
