<h2>4. System Architecture — Big Picture</h2>
<pre><code>RAW MICROSCOPE SLIDE IMAGE (.bmp)
         │
         ▼
   ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
   │          YOLOv8-Nano            │
   │       &quot;The Cell Hunter&quot;         │
   │  Detects all cells → bbox crops │
   └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                    │  Crops each cell
         ┌──────────┴──────────┐
         ▼                     ▼
  ┌─────────────┐    ┌───────────────────────┐
  │   U-Net     │    │    EfficientNet-B0    │
  │ &quot;Biologist&quot; │    │    &quot;Pathologist&quot;      │
  │             │    │                       │
  │ Pixel mask  │    │  Texture, chromatin   │
  │ Nuc vs Cyt  │    │  color pattern CNN    │
  └──────┬──────┘    └───────────┬───────────┘
         │                       │
         ▼                       ▼
  46 Morphological       5 CNN Probability
     Features              Features
         │                       │
         └──────────┬────────────┘
                    │  51 features fused
                    ▼
   ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
   │      SUPER ENSEMBLE             │
   │                                 │
   │  XGBoost  + LightGBM  +  RF    │
   │  (13 feats) (20 feats) (9 feats)│
   │                                 │
   │   HARD MAJORITY VOTE (2-of-3)   │
   └────────────────┬────────────────┘
                    ▼
             FINAL DIAGNOSIS
     + Confidence Score (avg. proba)
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h2>5. Pipeline: Phase-by-Phase Breakdown</h2>
<h3>Phase 1: Data Preprocessing (<code>1_Data_Preprocessing.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p>Converts the raw SIPaKMeD dataset into three distinct formatted datasets:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>For YOLO</strong> — Polygon <code>.dat</code> files → normalized YOLO <code>.txt</code> bounding boxes + <code>data.yaml</code></li>
<li><strong>For U-Net</strong> — Polygon boundaries → rasterized 3-class pixel masks (0=Background, 1=Cytoplasm, 2=Nucleus)</li>
<li><strong>For EfficientNet</strong> — Cropped cells sorted into class-labeled folders</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Output:</strong></p>
<pre><code>processed_data/
├── yolo_dataset/   (4,049 images + YOLO labels)
├── unet_dataset/   (crops + 3-channel masks)
└── cnn_dataset/    (class-sorted crops)
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 2: YOLOv8 Cell Detection (<code>2_YOLOv8_Training.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p><strong>Architecture:</strong> YOLOv8-Nano, pre-trained on MS-COCO, fine-tuned for single-class "cell" detection.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Parameter</th>
<th>Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Base Model</td>
<td>YOLOv8-Nano</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Epochs</td>
<td>50</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Image Size</td>
<td>640 × 640</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Task</td>
<td>Single-class detection</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Device</td>
<td>NVIDIA RTX 4050</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> <code>runs/detect/sipakmed_yolo/weights/best.pt</code></p>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 3: U-Net Semantic Segmentation (<code>3_UNet_Training.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p><strong>Architecture:</strong> U-Net with ResNet-34 encoder (ImageNet pre-trained), via <code>segmentation_models_pytorch</code>.</p>
<p>The <strong>Nucleus-to-Cytoplasm (NC) Ratio</strong> is the #1 clinical biomarker for cervical cancer. To compute it precisely, every single pixel must be classified — U-Net provides this pixel-perfect segmentation.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Parameter</th>
<th>Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Encoder</td>
<td>ResNet-34 (ImageNet)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Input Size</td>
<td>128 × 128</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Classes</td>
<td>3 (Background, Cytoplasm, Nucleus)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Loss</td>
<td>CrossEntropyLoss</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Optimizer</td>
<td>Adam</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Epochs</td>
<td>24 of 50 (Early Stopping)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Validation Accuracy</td>
<td><strong>~93.12%</strong></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> <code>trained_models/unet/unet_sipakmed.pth</code></p>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 4: EfficientNet-B0 Classification (<code>4_EfficientNet_Training.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p><strong>Architecture:</strong> EfficientNet-B0 (Google) with a replaced 5-class output head.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">cnn = models.efficientnet_b0(weights='IMAGENET1K_V1')
cnn.classifier[1] = nn.Linear(cnn.classifier[1].in_features, 5)
</code></pre>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Parameter</th>
<th>Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Input Size</td>
<td>224 × 224</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Classes</td>
<td>5</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Loss</td>
<td>CrossEntropyLoss</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Optimizer</td>
<td>Adam</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Augmentation</td>
<td>H/V flip, ±15° rotation, color jitter</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Epochs</td>
<td>21 of 50 (Early Stopping)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Validation Accuracy</td>
<td><strong>~97.41%</strong></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Output:</strong> <code>trained_models/cnn/efficientnet_sipakmed.pth</code></p>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 5: Enhanced Feature Extraction (<code>5_Feature_Extraction.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p>Passes all 4,049 cells through locked U-Net + EfficientNet to generate the 51-column feature matrix.</p>
<p><strong>Outputs:</strong>
- <code>extracted_features.csv</code> — original 13 features
- <code>extracted_features_enhanced.csv</code> — <strong>51 features</strong> (4,049 × 53 columns)</p>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 6: Individual Meta-Learners (<code>6_XGBoost.ipynb</code>, <code>7_LightGBM.ipynb</code>, <code>8_RandomForest.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p>Three classifiers independently trained on the 51-feature matrix with their own feature subsets selected via feature importance analysis.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Model</th>
<th>Features</th>
<th>Accuracy</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>XGBoost</td>
<td>13</td>
<td>99.80%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>LightGBM</td>
<td>20</td>
<td>99.73%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Random Forest</td>
<td>9</td>
<td>99.73%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 7: Super Ensemble (<code>9_Super_Ensemble.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p>Combines the three models into a <code>CervicalCancerSuperEnsemble</code> object with hard majority voting.</p>
<p><strong>Output:</strong>
- <code>trained_models/Super_Ensemble_Model.pkl</code> (3.17 MB)
- <code>trained_models/Super_Ensemble_Scaler.pkl</code> (2.67 KB)</p>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 8: Ablation &amp; Explainability (<code>10_Ablation_and_Explainability.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Ablation Study:</strong> Tests all 6 configurations (each model alone + ensemble) on clean and noise-corrupted data to prove the ensemble is more robust.</li>
<li><strong>Grad-CAM:</strong> Thermal heatmap showing EfficientNet's attention regions. Validates that red zones align with the nucleus, confirming the AI learned real cytology.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>Phase 9: Final Pipeline (<code>11_Final_Pipeline.ipynb</code>)</h3>
<p>Full end-to-end inference script. Mirrors the logic in <code>app_13.py</code> but in notebook form.</p>
<pre><code>Raw Slide → YOLO → U-Net → EfficientNet → 51 features → Super Ensemble → Diagnosis
</code></pre>
