<li>Runs YOLO on "Start Analysis" click</li>
<li>Progressively animates cyan bounding boxes as cells are detected</li>
<li>Active cell highlighted magenta during processing</li>
</ul>
<h4>Tab 2: Cellular Analysis <em>(per detected cell)</em></h4>
<p><strong>Row 1 — Images (3 columns):</strong>
- Raw cell crop
- U-Net mask (cyan = cytoplasm, dark blue = nucleus)
- Chromatin texture map (CLAHE + Inferno colormap on nucleus region)</p>
<p><strong>Row 2 — Charts (2 columns):</strong>
- <strong>Super Ensemble Confidence Bar Chart</strong> — horizontal, Reds for danger / Blues for benign
- <strong>Cellular Biomarker Radar Chart</strong> — spider plot of 5 normalized biomarkers:
  - NC Ratio, Circularity, Solidity, Entropy, Texture (GLCM Homogeneity)
  - Red fill for critical cells, Blue for benign</p>
<p><strong>HUD Status Bar:</strong> <code>DIAGNOSIS | NC_RATIO | ENSEMBLE CONFIDENCE</code></p>
<h4>Tab 3: Diagnostic Report</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>CRITICAL/NOMINAL badge</strong> with count of anomalous cells</li>
<li><strong>📊 Population Analytics:</strong></li>
<li>Donut Chart — class distribution across all detected cells</li>
<li>Scatter Plot — Nucleus Area vs. Cytoplasm Area, colored by diagnosis, sized by confidence</li>
<li><strong>🗄️ Comprehensive Feature Extraction Matrix:</strong></li>
<li>54-column table (Target, Diagnosis, Confidence + all 51 features)</li>
<li>Critical rows (DANGER_CLASSES) highlighted in <strong>red</strong> via <code>df.style.apply()</code></li>
</ul>
<h3>Key Engineering Fixes</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>CUDA OOM on 6GB GPU</td>
<td>All inference forced to CPU via <code>map_location="cpu"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Streamlit buffer exhaustion on rerun</td>
<td><code>.getvalue()</code> instead of <code>.read()</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>XGBoost GPU/CPU crash (Windows)</td>
<td><code>ensemble.xgb.get_booster().set_param({"device": "cpu"})</code> at load</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>StreamlitDuplicateElementId</code> in loop</td>
<td><code>key=f"bar_{idx}"</code> and <code>key=f"radar_{idx}"</code> per chart</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>GLCM memory explosion</td>
<td>Downscale nucleus to 64×64 before co-occurrence computation</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
